# The number of Swift tests this suite is expected to run, AT MINIMUM.
#
# Measured 2026-08-16 on main 7953828f: 283 tests across 36 files, 0 failures,
# 3.3 seconds. Until that day NOTHING ran them, and no register enumerated
# them, so they were never even scored UNWIRED.
#
# This is a FLOOR, not an equality. Adding tests must never fail the gate.
# Dropping below it must, because a suite that silently shrinks from 283 to 12
# exits 0 and prints the same green as a suite that did its job.
#
# Lowering this number is allowed and sometimes correct. Do it in the SAME
# commit that removes the tests, and say why in the message.
#
# Raised to 288 on 2026-08-18 (#839). MEASURED, not estimated: the swift-tests
# run on PR #840 printed
#     swift-tests: executed=288 failures=0 declared-floor=283
# The five new tests are ProgressDecoderTests' status-decoding cases, which
# pin that a STEP_END carrying status=timeout or status=error does not decode
# to .ok. Leaving the floor at 283 would have let those five be deleted with
# the gate still green, which is the same shape of defect the PR fixes.
#
# Raised to 318 on 2026-08-23 (v1.0.42 walk, finding 1). MEASURED, not
# estimated: the swift-tests run on PR #993 printed, on two different commits
# of that branch,
#     swift-tests: executed=318 failures=0 declared-floor=288
# The 21 new cases are AutoQuitAndKeepInstallerTests -- the auto-quit window,
# the offer-to-trash defaulting to KEEP (CX-52 trashed the app silently and
# unconditionally), the memory ceiling driven to RED at the 4.27 GB actually
# read off the box, and the bounded output buffer at the type level.
#
# The gap between 288 and 318 is wider than the 21 added here: the floor had
# not been raised since #839 and other tests landed in between. Stated rather
# than smoothed over -- 318 is the number the workflow printed, and it is the
# only number I can defend.
#
# Raised to 374 on 2026-09-16 (recovery-key / support-log defect sweep). The 36
# new cases cover: the recovery-key reveal surviving a FAILED install and the
# auto-quit refusing to close over an unacknowledged key; the fingerprint cache
